#
# Fixtures are oracles, checked byte-for-byte via tools/check_fixtures.py's
# SHA-256 comparison (INF-04, AGENTS.md §3). Without this file, a
# contributor with core.autocrlf=true (the common Windows default) gets
# their checkout of every fixture silently rewritten from the repo's LF to
# CRLF — invisible to `git status`/`git diff`, which normalize it back, but
# not to a byte-level hash. The result looks exactly like local fixture
# tampering (CONTENT CHANGED, wrong hash) without any of it being real,
# and undermines confidence in the guardrail that's supposed to catch the
# genuine version of that failure mode.
#
# `-text` disables any newline conversion for these paths, on every
# platform and regardless of a contributor's own autocrlf setting, so the
# working tree always matches the committed blob exactly.
fixtures/** -text
